body_clean:
**Godot version:**
322

**OS/device including version:**
Windows 10

**Issue description:**
I created a custom class PlayerInfo : Godot.Object and passed it as an argument to an RPC

RpcId(netId, nameof(_SetPlayerInfo), _MyPlayerInfo);

private void _SetPlayerInfo(PlayerInfo myPlayerInfo)
{
 //this method added myPlayerInfo to a dictionary, there was no error
}

when using the values of the dictionary godot crashes without any error.
I noticed that the typed of the PlayerInfo is Godot.EncodedObjectAsId as the parameter inside _SetPlayerInfo, and once you access any of the properties like myPlayerInfo.PlayerName the game crashes without any error

Maybe thats okey, that it converts it to that class.
But the bug is def. that it crashes without any error message.

Thanks

**Steps to reproduce:**
Create Class
public class PlayerInfo : Object.Godot

Pass as RPC param
RpcId(netId, nameof(_SetPlayerInfo), new PlayerInfo("someName", myNetId));

[Remote]
private void _SetPlayerInfo(PlayerInfo pInfo)
{
  GD.Print(pInfo.PlayerName);
}

**Minimal reproduction project:**
[Project.zip](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/files/5196255/Project.zip)

