[Bug]: [New headless] can't retrieve HTTPResponse from HTTP 401 pages

Environment:
Error string: net::ERR_INVALID_AUTH_CREDENTIALS
Puppeteer version: 19.7.5
Node version: 18.15.0
Package manager: npm
Package manager version: 9.5.0
Operating system: Windows

Bug expectation:
In old headless mode, `page.goto` retrieves `HTTPResponse` object from 401 pages. We were able to handle 401 pages just like 404 pages.

In new headless mode, `page.goto` throws Error: net::ERR_INVALID_AUTH_CREDENTIALS for 401 pages.  We aren't able to handle 401 pages just like 404 pages.

I'd expect that  `page.goto` retrieves `HTTPResponse` object from 401 pages in new headless.

If this is correct behaviour, please update <<URL>

> page.goto will not throw an error when any valid HTTP status code is returned by the remote server, including 404 "Not Found" and 500 "Internal Server Error". The status code for such responses can be retrieved by calling response.status().

Minimal, reproducible example:
```TypeScript
import {launch} from 'puppeteer';

(async () => {
    const url = '<URL>
    {
        console.log('Old headless');

        const browser = await launch({
            headless: true,
        });
        const page = await browser.newPage();
        const response = await page.goto(url);

        console.log('response:', response);
        console.log('status:', response.status());
    }

    console.log();

    {
        console.log('New headless');

        const browser = await launch({
            headless: 'new',
        });
        const page = await browser.newPage();
        const response = await page.goto(url);

        console.log('response:', response);
        console.log('status:', response.status());
    }
})();
```

