{"what steps will reproduce the bug?": "```javascript
const net = require("net")

const srv = net.createServer()

srv.on("connection", c => {
    const sock = new net.Socket({
        fd: c._handle.fd
    })
})

srv.listen(4444)
```", "how often does it reproduce? is there a required condition?": "No required condition (as far as I can tell).", "what is the expected behavior?": "That a new `net.Socket` instance is created which behaves exactly like the original instance (`c` in this case).", "what do you see instead?": "An error is thrown (EEXISTS):

```
net.js:337
        throw errnoException(err, 'open');
        ^

Error: open EEXIST
    at new Socket (net.js:337:15)
    at Server.<anonymous> (test.js:6:15)
    at Server.emit (events.js:315:20)
    at TCP.onconnection (net.js:1560:8) {
  errno: -17,
  code: 'EEXIST',
  syscall: 'open'
}
```", "additional information": ""}

{"tested versions": "- This is reproducible in v4.2.stable.official [46dc27791]", "system information": "Godot v4.2.stable - macOS 14.2.0 - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Apple M2 Pro - Apple M2 Pro (10 Threads)", "issue description": "When building a dedicated server (in this case a gateway) you will typically send an RPC call to a client with some response, such as a login response, and then disconnect the client. If you perform this function in Godot, the rpc_id call to the client will never be sent as the network.disconnect_peer() will terminate the client before the rpc call happens", "steps to reproduce": "Create a method where an rpc_id(client_id) is sent to a client followed immediately by a network.disconnect_peer(client_id). The disconnected peer will never receive the rpc call.

@rpc("any_peer", "call_local", "reliable")	
func return_login_response( player_id, result ):
	print("Sending login response to client %d" % player_id )
	rpc_id(player_id, "return_login_response", player_id, result )
	network.disconnect_peer(player_id)", "minimal reproduction project (mrp)": "The reproduction steps are not project dependent (e.g. the bug is visible in a brand new project)

N/A"}

