This breaks some test cases in Koa's test suite.

Node: `http://example.com/foo`
Deno: `/http://example.com/foo` <- notice the leading `/`

Steps to reproduce:
```ts
import http from "";

const server = http.createServer();

server.on("request", (request, res) => {
  res.end(request.url);
});

server.listen(8000);

http.get({
  host: "localhost",
  // This field is not parsed properly
  path: "http://example.com/foo",
  port: 8000,
}, async (res) => {
  let buf = "";
  res.setEncoding("utf8");
  res.on("data", (s) => {
    buf += s;
  });
  res.on("end", () => {
    console.log(buf);
  });
});
```

Version: Deno 1.44.4

