body_clean:
Our policy is to disable flaky tests if they are affecting trunk health. Dataloader tests have been quite serious offenders in terms of flakiness (see the long list of [disabled test issues](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22module%3A+dataloader%22)). I thought it would be good to start a high level conversation about what we can do to improve the reliability of the dataloader tests.

@mruberry suggests that we split out dataloader tests into a separate config so it is more clear when they fail. I also think that module-level retries are appropriate.

@vitaly-fedyunin, @ejguan: as module owners, who is the right POC to do this stuff?

cc @ezyang @gchanan @zou3519 @bdhirsh @SsnL @VitalyFedyunin @ejguan @NivekT

