{"description of the new feature / enhancement": "Some mechanism that would allow a pristine installation.  Any of a number of approaches could work as long as there was a clear distinction between preserving prior settings versus resetting to install defaults.  For example, it could be an option on install, or a special option in Settings, or a simple, clearly documented, extra manual step.  Whatever the approach, it should be easy to find in the documentation.  This should not prevent the preservation of current settings during an update or reinstall.

An ideal approach might also include listing the settings that are different (showing current v. default) -- or even an optional advanced step of accepting or removing each one from a list.  The actual comparison might be better done as a report in Settings, so it could be referred to at any time, not just install.  That report could also be repurposed and produced during the installation, if requested.  (If there is already a simple way to do a pristine install, this paragraph would be a seperate enhancement.)", "scenario when this would be used?": "In this particular case, I wanted a pristine installation of the current version to use to reproduce and document a bug/feature request (e.g., see Repair bug(?) in supporting info; or try setting the same shortcut for multiple PowerToys utilities).  I also wanted to check the current shortcut defaults.", "supporting information": "I tried to uninstall and install, but that preserved the settings (generally a good thing).  I could not find anything in the documentation wiki nor by searching Issues (although I suspect I overlooked an issue as I also did not find anything on preserving settings during install).  

I also tried the Repair option, but that failed to find the bootstrap msi (an issue to be researched and documented another day)."}

