fields_json:
{"godot version": "3.3.2-stable", "system information": "MacOS Bir Sur 11.4 - Radeon Pro 580X 8 GB", "issue description": "get_wordwrap_string_size result divided by font.get_height gives not correct line count if the text has no whitespace.
Text is shown correctly in RichTextLabel", "steps to reproduce": "I made a small project where you can see, that the line count should be 3 but the output is just 2.

this is the whole code, you can see that it grabs the size for the width from the RichTextLabel, so it should be 3 as well.

```
func _ready():
	var font:Font = $RichTextLabel.get_font("normal_font")
	var max_width = $RichTextLabel.rect_size.x
	calc_line_count(font, $RichTextLabel.bbcode_text, max_width)

func calc_line_count(font: Font, text: String, max_width: float):
	var text_dim: Vector2 = font.get_wordwrap_string_size(text, max_width)
	var line_count = text_dim.y / font.get_height()
	prints("Text", text)
	prints("max_wdith", max_width)
	prints("rect", text_dim)
	prints("line count", text_dim.y / font.get_height())
```", "minimal reproduction project": "[JapaneseLinecount.zip](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/files/6671199/JapaneseLinecount.zip)"}

body_clean:
Environment:
Alternatives considered: No

Describe the problem:
Sometimes style switching logic is placed in the parent component and controlled by switching the classNames. To avoid using the global CSS className, we need a utility to create a unique className and mark it as used.

Describe the proposed solution:
There is a proposal API:

```html
// Parent.svelte
<script>
import Child from './Child.svelte'
import { classname } from 'svelte/classname'

const luckyClassName = classname('lucky')
const unluckyClassName = classname('unlucky')

let isLucky = false

</script>

<Child class={isLucky ? luckyClassName : unluckyClassName} on:click={() => isLucky = !isLucky} />

<style>
// mark as used
.lucky {
  color: red;
}

// mark as used
.unlucky {
  color: blue;
}
</style>

```

Importance:
would make my life easier

